From 45cccd40165f72a271089faadace5a83f871c055 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Broyojo <dha@xoba.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:09:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] webpatch: Show only the graphics options Hadron's renderers
 read

The Compatibility page's Graphics panel was written for CrossOver. Under
Hadron, the backend choice (CX_GRAPHICS_BACKEND), both DLSS switches,
AVX2 for Rosetta, MSync and the high-resolution switch write launch
options that nothing reads: Hadron picks the renderer by the game's API,
has no D3DMetal and no NVIDIA libraries, runs x86 code with FEX, has no
MSync in its Wine and its own launch script.

Keep the Metal HUD and MetalFX upscaling, which DXMT reads, and say that
the upscaler is for Direct3D 10 and 11 games. Arguments that a removed
control wrote stay in the launch options untouched.
---
 dylib/feats/webpatch.c                  | 30 ++--------
 dylib/tests/panel-behavior/behavior.js  | 69 +++++++---------------
 dylib/tests/panel-behavior/switching.js | 76 ++++++++-----------------
 3 files changed, 52 insertions(+), 123 deletions(-)

